,"verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a GitHub trend-watching utility with disclosed local bookmarking behavior and no evidence of hidden execution, credential access, exfiltration, or destructive actions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Outbound network access to GitHub is proportionate to a trend-monitoring tool; no secrets, local auth/session stores, broad filesystem scans, or privileged system resources are requested.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact contains a markdown skill file and a JavaScript module, with no package install script, post-install hook, scheduled task, service setup, or remote payload execution.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The scope is generally disclosed, but the CLI documentation does not exactly match the code: `--bookmark` is documented as saving to a file, while the implemented `-b/--bookmarks` path lists bookmarks and the save helper is not wired into the CLI.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The code can persist bookmark data to a fixed local OpenClaw workspace path, which is purpose-aligned but should be understood before use; no cross-session agent rules, hooks, backdoors, or automatic startup persistence were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The documented purpose is to monitor GitHub Trending, filter projects, report trends, and manage bookmarks; the code fetches GitHub Trending, analyzes repository metadata, prints reports, and includes local bookmark read/write helpers.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Before installing, expect the skill to contact GitHub when run and to keep bookmark data locally if its bookmark helper is used. The documentation should be tightened around the bookmark CLI behavior and storage path, but the observed behavior is coherent with a trend-monitoring and bookmarking utility.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The external GitHub access and local bookmark storage are expected for this tool and are at least partially disclosed in the feature, option, and integration sections; the Feishu and daily memory references appear documented but not implemented in the inspected code.\n[SDI-4] expected: The bookmark persistence and `.md` filename versus JSON contents are real quality and clarity issues, but they do not show hidden or purpose-mismatched behavior.\n[AIG SARIF] expected: The static scan reported no T01-T09 findings, and the artifact inspection did not reveal instruction hijacking, remote payload execution, privilege escalation, tool spoofing, or system persistence.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031181312}}}}}